From: CJ Damsleth <kim@damsleth.no>
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: apple: no DMA direction for commands without a data transfer

Flush has no PRP list. The T6040 driver gave it dma_flags FROM_DEVICE, and
m1n1's old probe gave it both directions; ANS2 answered both with status 2
("fast decode err 0x7"; 211 write run 1, ticket 5006). Mainline apple.c, Yuka's
branch and Asahi's 7.2.12-2 all write dma_flags = 0 when prp1 is empty, and
m1n1 c16d3c74609976 (Sven Peter) says a direction on a command with no
transfer likely trips the PRP NULL check. Do the same here. Reads and writes,
and the TCB opcode, are unchanged, so the validated I/O path is untouched
(Flush's opcode is 0 either way).

Untested on T6040 hardware. Opt-in (NVME_FLUSH_NODMA=1); see ticket 5023.

Signed-off-by: CJ Damsleth <kim@damsleth.no>
---
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
@@ -336,7 +336,9 @@
 	tcb->length = cmd->rw.length;
 	tcb->command_id = tag;
 
-	if (nvme_is_write(cmd))
+	if (!cmd->common.dptr.prp1)
+		tcb->dma_flags = 0;
+	else if (nvme_is_write(cmd))
 		tcb->dma_flags = APPLE_ANS_TCB_DMA_TO_DEVICE;
 	else
 		tcb->dma_flags = APPLE_ANS_TCB_DMA_FROM_DEVICE;
